                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "El valor (numérico) que indica posición temporal en un sistema de referencia ordinal."@es ,
                                                                                               "The (numeric) value indicating position within a temporal coordinate system "@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#second
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#second> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                              owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription> ;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                                     rdfs:comment "Posición de segundo en un sistema calendario-reloj."@es ,
                                                  "Second position in a calendar-clock system."@en ;
                                     rdfs:label "second"@en ,
                                                "segundo"@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#seconds
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#seconds> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                               owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                      rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription> ;
                                      rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Longitud de, o elemento de la longitud de, una extensión temporal expresada en segundos."@es ,
                                                   "length of, or element of the length of, a temporal extent expressed in seconds"@en ;
                                      rdfs:label "duración en segundos"@es ,
                                                 "seconds duration"@en ;
                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.bipm.org/en/publications/si-brochure/second.html> .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#week
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#week> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                            owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription> ;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                   rdfs:comment "Número de semana en el año."@es ,
                                                "Week number within the year."@en ;
                                   rdfs:label "semana"@es ,
                                              "week"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Weeks are numbered differently depending on the calendar in use and the local language or cultural conventions (locale). ISO-8601 specifies that the first week of the year includes at least four days, and that Monday is the first day of the week. In that system, week 1 is the week that contains the first Thursday in the year."@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Las semanas están numeradas de forma diferente dependiendo del calendario en uso y de las convenciones lingüísticas y culturales locales (locale en inglés). El ISO-8601 especifica que la primera semana del año incluye al menos cuatro días, y que el lunes es el primer día de la semana. En ese sistema, la semana 1 es la semana que contiene el primer jueves del año."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#weeks
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#weeks> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                             owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription> ;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                                    rdfs:comment "Longitud de, o elemento de la longitud de, una extensión temporal expresada en semanas."@es ,
                                                 "length of, or element of the length of, a temporal extent expressed in weeks"@en ;
                                    rdfs:label "duración en semanas"@es ,
                                               "weeks duration"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#xsdDateTime
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#xsdDateTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                          rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeInterval> ;
                                          rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Valor de 'intervalo de fecha-hora' expresado como un valor compacto."@es ,
                                                       "Value of DateTimeInterval expressed as a compact value."@en ;
                                          rdfs:label "has XSD date-time"@en ,
                                                     "tiene fecha-hora XSD"@es ;
                                          owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Using xsd:dateTime in this place means that the duration of the interval is implicit: it corresponds to the length of the smallest non-zero element of the date-time literal. However, this rule cannot be used for intervals whose duration is more than one rank smaller than the starting time - e.g. the first minute or second of a day, the first hour of a month, or the first day of a year. In these cases the desired interval cannot be distinguished from the interval corresponding to the next rank up. Because of this essential ambiguity, use of this property is not recommended and it is deprecated."@en ,
                                                                                     "enUtilizando xsd:dateTime en este lugar significa que la duración del intervalo está implícita: se corresponde con la longitud del elemento más pequeño distinto de cero del literal fecha-hora. Sin embargo, esta regla no se puede utilizar para intervalos cuya duración es mayor que un rango más pequeño que el tiempo de comienzo - p.ej. el primer minuto o segundo del día, la primera hora del mes, o el primer día del año. En estos casos el intervalo deseado no se puede distinguir del intervalo correspondiente al próximo rango más alto. Debido a esta ambigüedad esencial, no se recomienda el uso de esta propiedad y está desaprobada." .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                            owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription> ;
                                   rdfs:comment """Posición de año en un sistema calendario-reloj.

l rango de esta propiedad no está especificado, por tanto, se puede reemplazar por cualquier representación específica de un año de calendario de un calendario cualquiera."""@es ,
                                                """Year position in a calendar-clock system.

The range of this property is not specified, so can be replaced by any specific representation of a calendar year from any calendar. """@en ;
                                   rdfs:label "year"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#years
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#years> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                             owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription> ;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                                    rdfs:comment "Longitud de, o elemento de la longitud de, una extensión temporal expresada en años."@es ,
                                                 "length of, or element of the length of, a temporal extent expressed in years"@en ;
                                    rdfs:label "duración en años"@es ,
                                               "years duration"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent> ;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                   rdfs:comment "The time at which an InstantaneousEvent occurred, in the form of xsd:dateTime."@en ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                   rdfs:label "atTime" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "qualified" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#sharesDefinitionWith> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#unqualifiedForm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#endedAtTime> ,
                                                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generatedAtTime> ,
                                                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#invalidatedAtTime> ,
                                                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#startedAtTime> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#endedAtTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#endedAtTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                        rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> ;
                                        rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                        rdfs:comment "The time at which an activity ended. See also prov:startedAtTime."@en ;
                                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                        rdfs:label "endedAtTime" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "starting-point" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorialNote> "It is the intent that the property chain holds: (prov:qualifiedEnd o prov:atTime) rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:endedAtTime."@en ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#qualifiedForm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generatedAtTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generatedAtTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                            rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                            rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                            rdfs:comment "The time at which an entity was completely created and is available for use."@en ;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                            rdfs:label "generatedAtTime" ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorialNote> "It is the intent that the property chain holds: (prov:qualifiedGeneration o prov:atTime) rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:generatedAtTime."@en ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#qualifiedForm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#invalidatedAtTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#invalidatedAtTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                              rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                              rdfs:comment "The time at which an entity was invalidated (i.e., no longer usable)."@en ;
                                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                              rdfs:label "invalidatedAtTime" ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorialNote> "It is the intent that the property chain holds: (prov:qualifiedInvalidation o prov:atTime) rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:invalidatedAtTime."@en ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#qualifiedForm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#startedAtTime
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#startedAtTime> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                          rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> ;
                                          rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                          rdfs:comment "The time at which an activity started. See also prov:endedAtTime."@en ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                          rdfs:label "startedAtTime" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "starting-point" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorialNote> "It is the intent that the property chain holds: (prov:qualifiedStart o prov:atTime) rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:startedAtTime."@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#qualifiedForm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atTime> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#value
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#value> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                  rdfs:label "value" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "Provides a value that is a direct representation of an entity."@en ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-attribute-value"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorialNote> "This property serves the same purpose as rdf:value, but has been reintroduced to avoid some of the definitional ambiguity in the RDF specification (specifically, 'may be used in describing structured values')."@en ,
                                                                            "The editor's definition comes from http://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-primer/#rdfvalue" .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/hasValue
<https://w3id.org/sulo/hasValue> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ,
                                          owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                 rdfs:comment "has value is the (only) data type attribute to store the values of information objects."@en ;
                                 rdfs:label "has value"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/versionIdentifier
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/versionIdentifier> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                                       rdfs:domain <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentVersion> ;
                                                                       rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A human-readable version identifier. The RDF IRI supplies the artifact identity."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "version identifier"@en .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Activity
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Activity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "A p-plan:Activity represents the execution process planned in a p-plan:Step" ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                      rdfs:label "Activity" .


###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Bundle
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Bundle> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Bundle> ;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                    rdfs:label "Bundle" ;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A p-plan:Bundle is a specific type of prov:Bundle that contains the provenance assertions of the execution of a p-plan:Plan" .


###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Entity
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Entity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                    rdfs:label "Entity" ;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "a p-plan:Entity represents the input of the execution of a p-plan:Activity. It corresponds to a p-plan:Variable." .


###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Plan> ;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                  rdfs:label "Plan" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A p-plan:Plan is a specific type of prov:Plan. It is composed of smaller steps that use and produce Variables." .


###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Step
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Step> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                  rdfs:label "Step" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A p-plan:Step represents the planned execution activity" .


###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Variable
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Variable> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                                      rdfs:label "Variable" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A p-plan:Variable represents a description of the input of the planned Activity (p-plan:Step)" .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeDescription
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeDescription> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription> ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS> ;
                                                                    owl:hasValue <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian>
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#day> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:gDay
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#month> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:gMonth
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:gYear
                                                                  ] ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Descripción de fecha y tiempo estructurada con valores separados para los diferentes elementos de un sistema calendario-reloj. El sistema de referencia temporal está fijado al calendario gregoriano, y el rango de las propiedades año, mes, día restringidas a los correspondientes tipos del XML Schema xsd:gYear, xsd:gMonth y xsd:gDay respectivamente."@es ,
                                                               "Description of date and time structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system. The temporal reference system is fixed to Gregorian Calendar, and the range of year, month, day properties restricted to corresponding XML Schema types xsd:gYear, xsd:gMonth and xsd:gDay, respectively."@en ;
                                                  rdfs:label "Date-Time description"@en ,
                                                             "descripción de fecha-tiempo"@es ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Descripción de fecha y tiempo estructurada con valores separados para los diferentes elementos de un sistema calendario-reloj. El sistema de referencia temporal está fijado al calendario gregoriano, y el rango de las propiedades año, mes, día restringidas a los correspondientes tipos del XML Schema xsd:gYear, xsd:gMonth y xsd:gDay respectivamente."@es ,
                                                                                                   "Description of date and time structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system. The temporal reference system is fixed to Gregorian Calendar, and the range of year, month, day properties restricted to corresponding XML Schema types xsd:gYear, xsd:gMonth and xsd:gDay, respectively."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeInterval
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeInterval> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval> ;
                                               rdfs:comment "'intervalo de fecha-hora' es una subclase de 'intervalo propio', definida utilizando el multi-elemento 'descripción de fecha-hora'."@es ,
                                                            "DateTimeInterval is a subclass of ProperInterval, defined using the multi-element DateTimeDescription."@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "Date-time interval"@en ,
                                                          "intervalo de fecha-hora"@es ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "'intervalo de fecha-hora' es una subclase de 'intervalo propio', definida utilizando el multi-elemento 'descripción de fecha-hora'."@es ,
                                                                                                "DateTimeInterval is a subclass of ProperInterval, defined using the multi-element DateTimeDescription."@en ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "'intervalo de fecha-hora' se puede utilizar sólo para un intervalo cuyos límites coinciden con un elemento de fecha-hora alineados con el calendario y la zona horaria indicados. Por ejemplo, aunque ambos tienen una duración de un día, el intervalo de 24 horas que empieza en la media noche del comienzo del 8 mayo en Europa Central se puede expresar como un 'intervalo de fecha-hora', el intervalo de 24 horas que empieza a las 1:30pm no."@es ,
                                                                                          ":DateTimeInterval can only be used for an interval whose limits coincide with a date-time element aligned to the calendar and timezone indicated. For example, while both have a duration of one day, the 24-hour interval beginning at midnight at the beginning of 8 May in Central Europe can be expressed as a :DateTimeInterval, but the 24-hour interval starting at 1:30pm cannot."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DayOfWeek
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DayOfWeek> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                        rdfs:comment "El día de la semana"@es ,
                                                     "The day of week"@en ;
                                        rdfs:label "Day of week"@en ,
                                                   "día de la semana"@es ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> """Remove enumeration from definition, in order to allow other days to be used when required in other calendars. 
NOTE: existing days are still present as members of the class, but the class membership is now open. 

In the original OWL-Time the following constraint appeared: 
  owl:oneOf (
      time:Monday
      time:Tuesday
      time:Wednesday
      time:Thursday
      time:Friday
      time:Saturday
      time:Sunday
    ) ;"""@en ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "El día de la semana"@es ,
                                                                                         "The day of week"@en ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "La pertenencia a la clase 'día de la semana' está abierta, para permitir longitudes de semana alternativas y diferentes nombres de días."@es ,
                                                                                   "Membership of the class :DayOfWeek is open, to allow for alternative week lengths and different day names."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Duration
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Duration> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalDuration> ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitType> ;
                                                         owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                       ] ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#numericDuration> ;
                                                         owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                       ] ;
                                       rdfs:comment "Duración de una extensión temporal expresada como un número escalado por una unidad temporal."@es ,
                                                    "Duration of a temporal extent expressed as a number scaled by a temporal unit"@en ;
                                       rdfs:label "Time duration"@en ,
                                                  "enduración de tiempo" ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Duración de una extensión temporal expresada como un número escalado por una unidad temporal."@es ,
                                                                                        "Duration of a temporal extent expressed as a number scaled by a temporal unit"@en ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Alternativa a 'descripción de tiempo' para proporcionar descripción soporte a una duración temporal diferente a utilizar un sistema de calendario/reloj."@es ,
                                                                                  "Alternative to time:DurationDescription to support description of a temporal duration other than using a calendar/clock system."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DurationDescription
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DurationDescription> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription> ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS> ;
                                                                    owl:hasValue <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian>
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#days> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hours> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#minutes> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#months> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#seconds> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#weeks> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#years> ;
                                                                    owl:allValuesFrom xsd:decimal
                                                                  ] ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Descripción de extensión temporal estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema de horario-calendario. El sistema de referencia temporal se fija al calendario gregoriano, y el intervalo de cada una de las propiedades numéricas se restringe a xsd:decimal."@es ,
                                                               "Description of temporal extent structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system. The temporal reference system is fixed to Gregorian Calendar, and the range of each of the numeric properties is restricted to xsd:decimal"@en ;
                                                  rdfs:label "Duration description"@en ,
                                                             "descripción de duración"@es ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Descripción de extensión temporal estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema de horario-calendario. El sistema de referencia temporal se fija al calendario gregoriano, y el intervalo de cada una de las propiedades numéricas se restringe a xsd:decimal."@es ,
                                                                                                   "Description of temporal extent structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system. The temporal reference system is fixed to Gregorian Calendar, and the range of each of the numeric properties is restricted to xsd:decimal"@en ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "En el calendario gregoriano la longitud de los meses no es fija. Por lo tanto, un valor como \"2,5 meses\" no se puede comparar exactamente con una duración similar expresada en términos de semanas o días."@es ,
                                                                                             "In the Gregorian calendar the length of the month is not fixed. Therefore, a value like \"2.5 months\" cannot be exactly compared with a similar duration expressed in terms of weeks or days."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalPosition> ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitType> ;
                                                                           owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#dayOfWeek> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#monthOfYear> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#timeZone> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#day> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#dayOfYear> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hour> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#minute> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#month> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#second> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#week> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ;
                                                         rdfs:comment "Descripción de fecha y hora estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema calendario-reloj."@es ,
                                                                      "Description of date and time structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system"@en ;
                                                         rdfs:label "Generalized date-time description"@en ,
                                                                    "descripción de fecha-hora generalizada"@es ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Description of date and time structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system"@en ,
                                                                                                          "enDescripción de fecha y hora estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema calendario-reloj." ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Algunas combinaciones de propiedades son redundantes - por ejemplo, dentro de un 'año' especificado si se proporciona 'día del año' entonces 'día' y 'mes' se pueden computar, y viceversa. Los valores individuales deberían ser consistentes entre ellos y con el calendario, indicado a través del valor de la propiedad 'tiene TRS'."@es ,
                                                                                                    "esSome combinations of properties are redundant - for example, within a specified :year if :dayOfYear is provided then :day and :month can be computed, and vice versa. Individual values should be consistent with each other and the calendar, indicated through the value of the :hasTRS property." .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDurationDescription> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalDuration> ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS> ;
                                                                           owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#days> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hours> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#minutes> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#months> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#seconds> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#weeks> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ,
                                                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#years> ;
                                                                           owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                         ] ;
                                                         rdfs:comment "Descripción de extensión temporal estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema de horario-calendario."@es ,
                                                                      "Description of temporal extent structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system."@en ;
                                                         rdfs:label "Generalized duration description"@en ,
                                                                    "descripción de duración generalizada"@es ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Descripción de extensión temporal estructurada con valores separados para los distintos elementos de un sistema de horario-calendario."@es ,
                                                                                                          "Description of temporal extent structured with separate values for the various elements of a calendar-clock system."@en ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "La extensión de una duración de tiempo expresada como una 'descripción de duración general' depende del Sistema de Referencia Temporal. En algunos calendarios la longitud de la semana o del mes no es constante a lo largo del año. Por tanto, un valor como \"25 meses\" puede no ser necesariamente ser comparado con un duración similar expresada en términos de semanas o días. Cuando se consideran calendarios que no están basados en el movimiento de la Tierra, se deben tomar incluso más precauciones en la comparación de duraciones."@es ,
                                                                                                    "The extent of a time duration expressed as a GeneralDurationDescription depends on the Temporal Reference System. In some calendars the length of the week or month is not constant within the year. Therefore, a value like \"2.5 months\" may not necessarily be exactly compared with a similar duration expressed in terms of weeks or days. When non-earth-based calendars are considered even more care must be taken in comparing durations."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Instant
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Instant> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalEntity> ;
                                      owl:disjointWith <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "A temporal entity with zero extent or duration"@en ,
                                                   "Una entidad temporal con una extensión o duración cero."@es ;
                                      rdfs:label "Time instant"@en ,
                                                 "instante de tiempo."@es ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal entity with zero extent or duration"@en ,
                                                                                       "Una entidad temporal con una extensión o duración cero."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Interval
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Interval> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalEntity> ;
                                       rdfs:comment "A temporal entity with an extent or duration"@en ,
                                                    "Una entidad temporal con una extensión o duración."@es ;
                                       rdfs:label "Time interval"@en ,
                                                  "intervalo de tiempo"@es ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal entity with an extent or duration"@en ,
                                                                                        "Una entidad temporal con una extensión o duración."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#January
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#January> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeDescription> ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitType> ;
                                                        owl:hasValue <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitMonth>
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#month> ;
                                                        owl:hasValue "--01"^^xsd:gMonth
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:label "January" ;
                                      owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote> "This class was present in the 2006 version of OWL-Time. It was presented as an example of how DateTimeDescription could be specialized, but does not belong in the revised ontology. " .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#MonthOfYear
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#MonthOfYear> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DateTimeDescription> ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitType> ;
                                                            owl:hasValue <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#unitMonth>
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#day> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hour> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#minute> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#month> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#second> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#week> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year> ;
                                                            owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "El mes del año."@es ,
                                                       "The month of the year"@en ;
                                          rdfs:label "Month of year"@en ,
                                                     "mes del año"@es ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "El mes del año."@es ,
                                                                                           "The month of the year"@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "Característica en riesgo - añadida en la revisión de 2017, y no utilizada todavía de forma amplia."@es ,
                                                                                              "Feature at risk - added in 2017 revision, and not yet widely used. "@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "La pertenencia a la clase 'mes del año' está abierta, a permitir calendarios anuales alternativos y diferentes nombres de meses."@es ,
                                                                                     "Membership of the class :MonthOfYear is open, to allow for alternative annual calendars and different month names."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Interval> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A temporal entity with non-zero extent or duration, i.e. for which the value of the beginning and end are different"@en ,
                                                          "Una entidad temporal con extensión o duración distinta de cero, es decir, para la cual los valores de principio y fin del intervalo son diferentes."@es ;
                                             rdfs:label "Proper interval"@en ,
                                                        "intervalo propio"@es ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal entity with non-zero extent or duration, i.e. for which the value of the beginning and end are different"@en ,
                                                                                              "Una entidad temporal con extensión o duración distinta de cero, es decir, para la cual los valores de principio y fin del intervalo son diferentes."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TRS
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TRS> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:comment """A temporal reference system, such as a temporal coordinate system (with an origin, direction, and scale), a calendar-clock combination, or a (possibly hierarchical) ordinal system. 

This is a stub class, representing the set of all temporal reference systems."""@en ,
                                               """Un sistema de referencia temporal, tal como un sistema de coordenadas temporales (con un origen, una dirección y una escala), una combinación calendario-reloj, o un sistema ordinal (posiblemente jerárquico).
        Esta clase comodín representa el conjunto de todos los sistemas de referencia temporal."""@es ;
                                  rdfs:label "Temporal Reference System"@en ,
                                             "sistema de referencia temporal"@es ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """A temporal reference system, such as a temporal coordinate system (with an origin, direction, and scale), a calendar-clock combination, or a (possibly hierarchical) ordinal system. 

This is a stub class, representing the set of all temporal reference systems."""@en ,
                                                                                   """Un sistema de referencia temporal, tal como un sistema de coordenadas temporales (con un origen, una dirección y una escala), una combinación calendario-reloj, o un sistema ordinal (posiblemente jerárquico).
    Esta clase comodín representa el conjunto de todos los sistemas de referencia temporal."""@es ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A taxonomy of temporal reference systems is provided in ISO 19108:2002 [ISO19108], including (a) calendar + clock systems; (b) temporal coordinate systems (i.e. numeric offset from an epoch); (c) temporal ordinal reference systems (i.e. ordered sequence of named intervals, not necessarily of equal duration)."@en ,
                                                                             "En el ISO 19108:2002 [ISO19108] se proporciona una taxonomía de sistemas de referencia temporal, incluyendo (a) sistemas de calendario + reloj; (b) sistemas de coordenadas temporales (es decir, desplazamiento numérico a partir de una época); (c) sistemas de referencia ordinales temporales (es decir, secuencia ordenada de intervalos nombrados, no necesariamente de igual duración)."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalDuration
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalDuration> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:comment "Extensión de tiempo; duración de un intervalo de tiempo independiente de su posición de inicio particular."@es ,
                                                            "Time extent; duration of a time interval separate from its particular start position"@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "Temporal duration"@en ,
                                                          "duración temporal"@es ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Extensión de tiempo; duración de un intervalo de tiempo independiente de su posición de inicio particular."@es ,
                                                                                                "Time extent; duration of a time interval separate from its particular start position"@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalEntity
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalEntity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                   owl:unionOf ( <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Instant>
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Interval>
                                                                               )
                                                                 ] ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A temporal interval or instant."@en ,
                                                          "Un intervalo temporal o un instante."@es ;
                                             rdfs:label "Temporal entity"@en ,
                                                        "entidad temporal"@es ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal interval or instant."@en ,
                                                                                              "Un intervalo temporal o un instante."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalPosition
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalPosition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                 owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasTRS> ;
                                                                 owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                               ] ;
                                               rdfs:comment "A position on a time-line"@en ,
                                                            "Una posición sobre una línea de tiempo."@es ;
                                               rdfs:label "Temporal position"@en ,
                                                          "posición temporal"@es ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A position on a time-line"@en ,
                                                                                                "Una posición sobre una línea de tiempo."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalUnit
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalUnit> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalDuration> ;
                                           rdfs:comment "A standard duration, which provides a scale factor for a time extent, or the granularity or precision for a time position."@en ,
                                                        "Una duración estándar, que proporciona un factor de escala para una extensión de tiempo, o la granularidad o precisión para una posición de tiempo."@es ;
                                           rdfs:label "Temporal unit"@en ,
                                                      "unidad de tiempo"@es ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> """Remove enumeration from definition, in order to allow other units to be used when required in other coordinate systems. 
NOTE: existing units are still present as members of the class, but the class membership is now open. 

In the original OWL-Time the following constraint appeared: 
  owl:oneOf (
      time:unitSecond
      time:unitMinute
      time:unitHour
      time:unitDay
      time:unitWeek
      time:unitMonth
      time:unitYear
    ) ;"""@en ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A standard duration, which provides a scale factor for a time extent, or the granularity or precision for a time position."@en ,
                                                                                            "Una duración estándar, que proporciona un factor de escala para una extensión de tiempo, o la granularidad o precisión para una posición de tiempo."@es ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "La pertenencia de la clase 'unidad de tiempo' está abierta, para permitir otras unidades de tiempo utilizadas en algunas aplicaciones técnicas (por ejemplo, millones de años o el mes Baha'i)."@es ,
                                                                                      "Membership of the class TemporalUnit is open, to allow for other temporal units used in some technical applications (e.g. millions of years, Baha'i month)."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TimePosition
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TimePosition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalPosition> ,
                                                           [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                             owl:unionOf ( [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                             owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#nominalPosition> ;
                                                                             owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                           ]
                                                                           [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                             owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#numericPosition> ;
                                                                             owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                                           ]
                                                                         )
                                                           ] ;
                                           rdfs:comment "A temporal position described using either a (nominal) value from an ordinal reference system, or a (numeric) value in a temporal coordinate system. "@en ,
                                                        "Una posición temporal descrita utilizando bien un valor (nominal) de un sistema de referencia ordinal, o un valor (numérico) en un sistema de coordenadas temporales."@es ;
                                           rdfs:label "Time position"@en ,
                                                      "posición de tiempo"@es ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A temporal position described using either a (nominal) value from an ordinal reference system, or a (numeric) value in a temporal coordinate system. "@en ,
                                                                                            "Una posición temporal descrita utilizando bien un valor (nominal) de un sistema de referencia ordinal, o un valor (numérico) en un sistema de coordenadas temporales."@es .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TimeZone
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TimeZone> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:comment """A Time Zone specifies the amount by which the local time is offset from UTC. 
	A time zone is usually denoted geographically (e.g. Australian Eastern Daylight Time), with a constant value in a given region. 
The region where it applies and the offset from UTC are specified by a locally recognised governing authority."""@en ,
                                                    """Un huso horario especifica la cantidad en que la hora local está desplazada con respecto a UTC.
        Un huso horario normalmente se denota geográficamente (p.ej. el horario de verano del este de Australia), con un valor constante en una región dada.
        La región donde aplica y el desplazamiento desde UTC las especifica una autoridad gubernamental localmente reconocida."""@es ;
                                       rdfs:label "Time Zone"@en ,
                                                  "huso horario"@es ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """A Time Zone specifies the amount by which the local time is offset from UTC. 
	A time zone is usually denoted geographically (e.g. Australian Eastern Daylight Time), with a constant value in a given region. 
The region where it applies and the offset from UTC are specified by a locally recognised governing authority."""@en ,
                                                                                        """Un huso horario especifica la cantidad en que la hora local está desplazada con respecto a UTC.
    Un huso horario normalmente se denota geográficamente (p.ej. el horario de verano del este de Australia), con un valor constante en una región dada.
    La región donde aplica y el desplazamiento desde UTC las especifica una autoridad gubernamental localmente reconocida."""@es ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote> """En la versión original de OWL-Time de 2006, se definió, en un espacio de nombres diferente \"http://www.w3.org/2006/timezone#\", la clase 'huso horario', con varias propiedades específicas correspondientes a un modelo específico de huso horario.
    En la versión actual hay una clase con el mismo nombre local en el espacio de nombres de OWL-Time, eliminando la dependencia del espacio de nombres externo.
    Un axioma de alineación permite que los datos codificados de acuerdo con la versión anterior sean consistentes con la ontología actualizada."""@es ,
                                                                                         """esIn the original 2006 version of OWL-Time, the TimeZone class, with several properties corresponding to a specific model of time-zones, was defined in a separate namespace \"http://www.w3.org/2006/timezone#\". 

In the current version a class with same local name is put into the main OWL-Time namespace, removing the dependency on the external namespace. 

An alignment axiom 
	tzont:TimeZone rdfs:subClassOf time:TimeZone . 
allows data encoded according to the previous version to be consistent with the updated ontology. """ ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> """A designated timezone is associated with a geographic region. However, for a particular region the offset from UTC often varies seasonally, and the dates of the changes may vary from year to year. The timezone designation usually changes for the different seasons (e.g. Australian Eastern Standard Time vs. Australian Eastern Daylight Time). Furthermore, the offset for a timezone may change over longer timescales, though its designation might not.  

Detailed guidance about working with time zones is given in http://www.w3.org/TR/timezone/ ."""@en ,
                                                                                  "An ontology for time zone descriptions was described in [owl-time-20060927] and provided as RDF in a separate namespace tzont:. However, that ontology was incomplete in scope, and the example datasets were selective. Furthermore, since the use of a class from an external ontology as the range of an ObjectProperty in OWL-Time creates a dependency, reference to the time zone class has been replaced with the 'stub' class in the normative part of this version of OWL-Time."@en ,
                                                                                  """Un huso horario designado está asociado con una región geográfica. Sin embargo, para una región particular el desplazamiento desde UTC a menudo varía según las estaciones, y las fechas de los cambios pueden variar de un año a otro. La designación de huso horario  normalmente cambia de una estación a otra (por ejemplo, el horario estándar frente al horario de verano ambos del este de Australia). Además, del desplazamiento para un huso horario puede cambiar sobre escalas de tiempo mayores, aunque su designación no lo haga.
    Se puede encontrar una guía detallada sobre el funcionamiento de husos horarios en http://www.w3.org/TR/timezone/.\"@es , \"En [owl-time-20060927] se describió una ontología para descripciones de husos horarios, y se proporcionó en un espacio de nombres separado tzont:. Sin embargo, dicha ontología estaba incompleta en su alcance, y el ejemplo de conjuntos de datos (datasets) era selectivo. Además, puesto que el uso de una clase de una ontología externa como el rango de una propiedad de objeto en OWL-Time crea una dependencia, la referencia a la clase huso horario se ha reemplazado por una clase que viene a ser un \"cajón de sastre\" en la en la parte normativa de esta versión de OWL-Time."""@es ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "En esta implementación 'huso horario' no tiene definidas propiedades. Se debería pensar como una superclase \"abstracta\" de todas las implementaciones de huso horario específicas."@es ,
                                                                                       "esIn this implementation TimeZone has no properties defined. It should be thought of as an 'abstract' superclass of all specific timezone implementations." .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Year
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Year> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#DurationDescription> ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#days> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hours> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#minutes> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#months> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#seconds> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#weeks> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#years> ;
                                                     owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                   ] ;
                                   rdfs:comment "Year duration" ;
                                   rdfs:label "Year"@en ;
                                   owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Year duration" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote> """Year was proposed in the 2006 version of OWL-Time as an example of how DurationDescription could be specialized to allow for a duration to be restricted to a number of years. 

It is deprecated in this edition of OWL-Time. """ ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Anno"@it ,
                                                                                   "Année (calendrier)"@fr ,
                                                                                   "Ano"@pt ,
                                                                                   "Año"@es ,
                                                                                   "Jaar"@nl ,
                                                                                   "Jahr"@de ,
                                                                                   "Rok"@pl ,
                                                                                   "Year"@en ,
                                                                                   "Год"@ru ,
                                                                                   "سنة"@ar ,
                                                                                   "年"@ja ,
                                                                                   "年"@zh .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process> ;
                                     owl:disjointWith <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                     rdfs:label "Activity" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "starting-point" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#constraints> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-constraints-20130430/#prov-dm-constraints-fig"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "An activity is something that occurs over a period of time and acts upon or with entities; it may include consuming, processing, transforming, modifying, relocating, using, or generating entities." ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-Activity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-Activity"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  owl:disjointWith <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent> ;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                  rdfs:label "Agent" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "starting-point" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "An agent is something that bears some form of responsibility for an activity taking place, for the existence of an entity, or for another agent's activity. "@en ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-agent"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-Agent"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#AgentInfluence
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#AgentInfluence> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Influence> ;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                           rdfs:label "AgentInfluence" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#editorsDefinition> "AgentInfluence is the capacity of an agent to have an effect on the character, development, or behavior of another by means of attribution, association, delegation, or other."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Association
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Association> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#AgentInfluence> ;
                                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                        rdfs:label "Association" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "An activity association is an assignment of responsibility to an agent for an activity, indicating that the agent had a role in the activity. It further allows for a plan to be specified, which is the plan intended by the agent to achieve some goals in the context of this activity."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Bundle
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Bundle> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Bundle" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A bundle is a named set of provenance descriptions, and is itself an Entity, so allowing provenance of provenance to be expressed."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Collection
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Collection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                       rdfs:label "Collection" ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A collection is an entity that provides a structure to some constituents, which are themselves entities. These constituents are said to be member of the collections."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#EmptyCollection
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#EmptyCollection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Collection> .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Object> ;
                                   owl:disjointWith <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent> ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Entity" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "starting-point" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#constraints> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-constraints-20130430/#prov-dm-constraints-fig"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "An entity is a physical, digital, conceptual, or other kind of thing with some fixed aspects; entities may be real or imaginary. "@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-entity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-Entity"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Influence
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Influence> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                      rdfs:label "Influence" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "Influence is the capacity of an entity, activity, or agent to have an effect on the character, development, or behavior of another by means of usage, start, end, generation, invalidation, communication, derivation, attribution, association, or delegation."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#InstantaneousEvent> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process> ;
                                               rdfs:comment "An instantaneous event, or event for short, happens in the world and marks a change in the world, in its activities and in its entities. The term 'event' is commonly used in process algebra with a similar meaning. Events represent communications or interactions; they are assumed to be atomic and instantaneous."@en ;
                                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                               rdfs:label "InstantaneousEvent" ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Instantaneous Event"@en ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "qualified" ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "entities-activities" ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#constraints> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-constraints-20130430/#dfn-event"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                               <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "The PROV data model is implicitly based on a notion of instantaneous events (or just events), that mark transitions in the world. Events include generation, usage, or invalidation of entities, as well as starting or ending of activities. This notion of event is not first-class in the data model, but it is useful for explaining its other concepts and its semantics."@en .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Location
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Location> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/SpatialObject> ;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                     rdfs:label "Location" ;
                                     rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#atLocation> ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote> "I made prov:Location a subclass of sulo:Spatial_Object MD 7/20/26"@en ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A location can be an identifiable geographic place (ISO 19112), but it can also be a non-geographic place such as a directory, row, or column. As such, there are numerous ways in which location can be expressed, such as by a coordinate, address, landmark, and so forth."@en ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-attribute-location"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-attribute"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Organization
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Organization> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> ;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                         rdfs:label "Organization" ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "An organization is a social or legal institution such as a company, society, etc." ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-agent"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-types"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Person
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Person> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Person" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "Person agents are people."@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-agent"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-types"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Plan
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Plan> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ;
                                 rdfs:comment "There exist no prescriptive requirement on the nature of plans, their representation, the actions or steps they consist of, or their intended goals. Since plans may evolve over time, it may become necessary to track their provenance, so plans themselves are entities. Representing the plan explicitly in the provenance can be useful for various tasks: for example, to validate the execution as represented in the provenance record, to manage expectation failures, or to provide explanations."@en ;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                 rdfs:label "Plan" ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ,
                                                                      "qualified" ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A plan is an entity that represents a set of actions or steps intended by one or more agents to achieve some goals." ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-Association"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-Association"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Role
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Role> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                 rdfs:label "Role" ;
                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#hadRole> ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "qualified" ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A role is the function of an entity or agent with respect to an activity, in the context of a usage, generation, invalidation, association, start, and end."@en ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-attribute-role"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-attribute"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#> ;
                                          rdfs:label "Software Agent"@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#category> "expanded" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#component> "agents-responsibility" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#definition> "A software agent is running software."@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#dm> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-agent"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#n> "http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-types"^^xsd:anyURI .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Capability
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Capability> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature> ;
                                   rdfs:comment "A capability is a feature that describes what an entity is able to do, under some set of circumstances."@en ;
                                   rdfs:label "capability" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the capability to fly, the capabilty to reduce the activation energy of a chemical reaction, the capability to reason"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Capability"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Collection
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Collection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasItem> ;
                                                     owl:allValuesFrom owl:Thing
                                                   ] ;
                                   owl:disjointWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/Quantity> ;
                                   rdfs:comment "A collection is an information object for which there may be zero or more items."@en ;
                                   rdfs:label "collection"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "a stamp collection, a murder of crows, the arm of a clinical trial"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Collection"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An information object that aggregates or organizes other information objects. This class is not intended as a general superclass for social groups, physical aggregates, organizations, or arbitrary mathematical sets. MD 7/15/26"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Duration
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Duration> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Time> ,
                                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                   owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasValue> ;
                                                   owl:someValuesFrom [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                                        owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
                                                                        owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 0.0
                                                                                               ]
                                                                                             )
                                                                      ]
                                                 ] ;
                                 rdfs:comment "Duration is a temporal quantity that represents the extent or (non-negative) amount of time that elapses between two temporal points, typically the start and end of a time interval."@en ;
                                 rdfs:label "duration"@en ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Duration"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/EndTime
<https://w3id.org/sulo/EndTime> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInstant> ;
                                owl:disjointWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/StartTime> ;
                                rdfs:comment "an end time is a time instant at the end of a process/time interval."@en ;
                                rdfs:label "end time"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "End Time"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Object> ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/isFeatureOf> ;
                                                  owl:someValuesFrom [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/sulo/Object>
                                                                                     <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process>
                                                                                   )
                                                                     ]
                                                ] ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                  owl:allValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature>
                                                ] ;
                                owl:disjointWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/SpatialObject> ;
                                owl:disjointUnionOf ( <https://w3id.org/sulo/Capability>
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject>
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/Quality>
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/Role>
                                                    ) ;
                                rdfs:comment "A feature is any characteristic that stems from the intrisinc structure and/or context"@en ;
                                rdfs:label "feature"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the capability to fly, a collection of cards, a measured height of 170cm."@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Feature"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject
<https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature> ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                            owl:allValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject>
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasValue> ;
                                                            owl:allValuesFrom rdfs:Literal
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "an information object is a feature that represents, is about, or encodes some information."@en ;
                                          rdfs:label "information object"@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Information Object"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Object
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Object> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                                    owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process>
                                                                  ]
                                               ] ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                 owl:allValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Object>
                                               ] ;
                               owl:disjointWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process> ;
                               rdfs:comment "An object is an entity that maintains its identity through time, and does not have processes as its parts." ;
                               rdfs:label "object"@en ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "a heart, the function to pump blood, the role of a doctor"@en ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Object"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Process
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Process> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                  owl:allValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Process>
                                                ] ;
                                rdfs:comment "a process is a entity that unfolds in time, has temporal parts, and has objects that participate in the process."@en ;
                                rdfs:label "process"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the process of diagnosing a problem condition, the process of walking down the street, the process of teaching a class"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Process"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Quality
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Quality> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature> ;
                                rdfs:comment "A quality is a feature that is intrinsically associated with its bearer (or its parts)."@en ,
                                             "the color of an apple, the smoothness of skin, the brightness of a star, the speed of an event"@en ;
                                rdfs:label "quality"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Quality"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Quantity
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Quantity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ,
                                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                   owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                   owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Unit>
                                                 ] ;
                                 rdfs:comment "A quantity is an information object that represents the magnitude (and unit) of an object or process."@en ;
                                 rdfs:label "quantity"@en ;
                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Quantity"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Role
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Role> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature> ;
                             rdfs:comment "A role is a feature that describes a context-dependent behaviour."@en ;
                             rdfs:label "role"@en ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "a teacher, a student, a catalyst, a substrate, a product, a patient"@en ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Role"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/SpatialObject
<https://w3id.org/sulo/SpatialObject> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Object> ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                        owl:allValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/SpatialObject>
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment "A spatial object is an object that occupies space"@en ;
                                      rdfs:label "spatial object"@en ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "a mountain, a planet, a photon, the lining of the stomach, the cavity of the stomach, the space between mars and earth"@en ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Spatial Object"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/StartTime
<https://w3id.org/sulo/StartTime> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInstant> ;
                                  rdfs:comment "a start time is a time instant at the beginning of a process/time interval."@en ;
                                  rdfs:label "start time"@en ;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Start Time"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Time
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Time> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Quantity> ;
                             owl:disjointWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/Unit> ;
                             owl:disjointUnionOf ( <https://w3id.org/sulo/Duration>
                                                   <https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInstant>
                                                   <https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInterval>
                                                 ) ;
                             rdfs:comment "time is a quantity pertaining to the duration of some interval of time or a particular instant of time (against some frame of reference)."@en ;
                             rdfs:label "time"@en ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Time"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInstant
<https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInstant> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Time> ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasValue> ;
                                                      owl:allValuesFrom [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                                          owl:unionOf ( xsd:dateTime
                                                                                        xsd:dateTimeStamp
                                                                                      )
                                                                        ]
                                                    ] ;
                                    rdfs:comment "time instant is a quantity of time a particular moment in time."@en ;
                                    rdfs:label "time instant"@en ;
                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Time Instant"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInterval
<https://w3id.org/sulo/TimeInterval> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Time> ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                       owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasDirectPart> ;
                                                       owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/EndTime>
                                                     ] ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                       owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasDirectPart> ;
                                                       owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/StartTime>
                                                     ] ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                       owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                       owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Duration>
                                                     ] ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                       owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> ;
                                                       owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/sulo/Unit>
                                                     ] ;
                                     rdfs:comment "A time interval is a quantity for a continuous and bounded extent of time, characterized by a start time and an end time."@en ;
                                     rdfs:label "time interval" ;
                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Time Interval"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/sulo/Unit
<https://w3id.org/sulo/Unit> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/sulo/Quantity> ;
                             rdfs:comment "a unit is a standardized quantity that is used as a reference for a particular quantity."@en ;
                             rdfs:label "unit" ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Unit"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationPlan
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationPlan> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A plan for collaboration between supply-chain participants. Use isStepOfPlan and isVariableOfPlan for its steps and resource variables."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Collaboration plan"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationRole
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationRole> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Role> ,
                                                                                       <https://w3id.org/sulo/Role> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A context-dependent function in a collaboration. Assign a role instance to an agent through PlannedAssignment or, for an execution, a PROV Association with hadRole."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Collaboration role"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Step> ,
                                                                                       <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                       <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A planned step description. It is an information object, not an occurrence. Actual performances are StepExecution instances linked with correspondsToStep."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Collaboration step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CommunicationStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CommunicationStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A planned communication task, which may include sending a request and awaiting a reply. Input/output dependencies can therefore be cyclic at this abstraction level without defining a cyclic control-flow sequence."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Communication step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ConditionalTransition
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ConditionalTransition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                           rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StepTransition> ;
                                                                           rdfs:comment "A possible transition with an explicit DecisionCondition. Missing conditions are incomplete data, not unconditional permission to proceed."@en ;
                                                                           rdfs:label "Conditional transition"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ContributionStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ContributionStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                      <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                      rdfs:comment "A planned step that produces a participant contribution to a draft or proposal."@en ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "Contribution step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionCondition
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionCondition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                       <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "A declarative condition requiring the result in conditionVariable to have expectedOutcome. This vocabulary records the condition; it does not evaluate it."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Decision condition"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionOutcome
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionOutcome> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                     <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                     rdfs:comment "An outcome value for a decision. Approved and Rejected are supplied as distinct reusable values; further values may be added."@en ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Decision outcome"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionResult
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionResult> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Entity> ,
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "An actual decision artifact, linked to its DecisionVariable by correspondsToVariable, its subject document by aboutVersion, and its outcome by hasOutcome."@en ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Decision result"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionVariable
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DecisionVariable> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Variable> ;
                                                                      rdfs:comment "A planned slot for a decision result produced by a review or vote. Branch conditions refer to this slot and the expected outcome."@en ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "Decision variable"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentSeries
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentSeries> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "The continuing document identity that groups versions through versionOf. Individual versions remain distinct artifacts."@en ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Document series"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentVariable
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentVariable> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Variable> ;
                                                                      rdfs:comment "A planned input or output slot for one document version or contribution. It is not the actual document artifact."@en ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "Document variable"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentVersion
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DocumentVersion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Entity> ,
                                                                                     <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                     rdfs:comment "A particular document snapshot or contribution artifact. Use correspondsToVariable, versionOf and previousVersion to distinguish its planned slot, document series and revision lineage."@en ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Document version"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DraftingStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/DraftingStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                  <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                  rdfs:comment "A planned step that produces an initial draft from its stated inputs."@en ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "Drafting step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EndEventStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EndEventStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EventStep> ;
                                                                  owl:disjointWith <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StartEventStep> ;
                                                                  rdfs:comment "A planned end event for a participant path, not necessarily the end of every participant in the collaboration."@en ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "End event step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EventStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EventStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                               rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ;
                                                               owl:disjointWith <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                               rdfs:comment "A planned workflow event or milestone. This is a description in a plan, not an actual prov:InstantaneousEvent or time:Instant. eventForRole identifies its participant lane."@en ;
                                                               rdfs:label "Event step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ExclusiveChoice
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ExclusiveChoice> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                     <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                     rdfs:comment "An explicitly modeled choice grouping alternative ConditionalTransitions. The alternatives should share the stated choiceAfterStep and have explicit conditions. Runtime branch selection and completeness checks belong to a controller or human."@en ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Exclusive choice"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/LeadSupplierRole
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/LeadSupplierRole> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationRole> ;
                                                                      rdfs:comment "The role of leading this collaboration; it is not a permanent classification of the organization."@en ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "Lead supplier role"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/Message
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/Message> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Entity> ,
                                                                             <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                             rdfs:comment "An actual message artifact, with sender, recipient and payload. Generation and use by actual activities are expressed using PROV."@en ;
                                                             rdfs:label "Message"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/MessageVariable
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/MessageVariable> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Variable> ;
                                                                     rdfs:comment "A planned message slot, with contextual sender/receiver roles and an optional payload variable. It is not a sent message."@en ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Message variable"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PartnerReplacementStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PartnerReplacementStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                            rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                            <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                            rdfs:comment "A planned step to replace or invite a new collaboration partner."@en ;
                                                                            rdfs:label "Partner replacement step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PartnerRole
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PartnerRole> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationRole> ;
                                                                 rdfs:comment "The role of an invited or participating partner in this collaboration."@en ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Partner role"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PlannedAssignment
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/PlannedAssignment> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                       <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                       rdfs:comment "An intended agent/role assignment for a planned step. Use assignmentForStep, assignedAgent and assignedRole. This is not a PROV Association and creates no actual wasAssociatedWith assertion."@en ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Planned assignment"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ReviewStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ReviewStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                rdfs:comment "A planned evaluation or vote on a document version; its decision output is represented by a DecisionVariable."@en ;
                                                                rdfs:label "Review step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/RevisionStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/RevisionStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                  <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                  rdfs:comment "A planned step that incorporates inputs into a new document version. Use a new output variable rather than overwriting the input version."@en ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "Revision step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StartEventStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StartEventStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/EventStep> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "A planned start event. triggeredByVariable describes the planned information whose arrival triggers the event; it does not generate that information."@en ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Start event step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StepExecution
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StepExecution> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Activity> ;
                                                                   rdfs:comment "An actual performance of a planned step. Through PROV Activity it is a SULO Process. Use qualifiedAssociation for agents and roles, used/wasGeneratedBy for artifacts, and OWL-Time endpoint paths for dated intervals."@en ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "Step execution"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StepTransition
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/StepTransition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> ,
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/sulo/InformationObject> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "An explicitly modeled possible control-flow transition from transitionFrom to transitionTo. It does not assert actual execution or temporal precedence."@en ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Step transition"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/SubmissionStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/SubmissionStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ,
                                                                                    <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "A planned submission of an agreed document to its recipient."@en ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Submission step"@en .


###  https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/TaskStep> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep> ;
                                                              rdfs:comment "A planned unit of work in a collaboration. Distinguished from a planned event; actual performances are StepExecution individuals."@en ;
                                                              rdfs:label "Task step"@en .


#################################################################
#    Individuals
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/net/p-plan#
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                       owl:Thing ;
                              <https://w3id.org/sulo/contains> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                              <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                              <https://w3id.org/sulo/isIn> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ;
                              <https://w3id.org/sulo/isPartOf> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> .


###  http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian
<http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/contains> <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian> ;
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/hasPart> <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian> ;
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/isIn> <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian> ;
                                                      <https://w3id.org/sulo/isPartOf> <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/ISO-8601/0/Gregorian> .


###  http://www.w3.org/2006/time#American_Civil_War
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#American_Civil_War> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
